Twist Hacking Guide
====================

Copyright (C) 2026 Chris

This file contains guidelines for contributing to Twist.

Reporting Bugs
--------------

When reporting bugs, please include:

  1. The version of Twist you are using
  2. The operating system and version
  3. The hardware architecture
  4. A complete description of the problem
  5. The exact steps to reproduce the problem
  6. Any relevant configuration or environment settings

Bugs can be reported to <chris@localhost>.

Submitting Patches
------------------

Patches are welcome!  Please follow these guidelines when submitting patches:

  1. Follow the existing coding style in the project
  2. Include a ChangeLog entry for your changes
  3. Update NEWS if the change is user-visible
  4. Keep changes focused and minimal
  5. Include a clear description of the problem and solution
  6. Use the same license (GPLv3+) for all new code
  7. Ensure all new files have appropriate copyright notices

To submit a patch, you can:

  - Email it to <chris@localhost>
  - Use a pull request if the project uses a version control system
    that supports them

Please include the following information in your submission:

  - Your name and email address
  - A description of the change
  - The rationale for the change
  - Any testing you have performed

Coding Standards
----------------

Twist follows GNU coding standards where applicable.  Key points:

  1. Use consistent indentation (preferably 2 or 4 spaces, no tabs)
  2. Limit lines to 79 characters where possible
  3. Use descriptive variable and function names
  4. Comment your code, but prefer clear code over comments
  5. Include copyright notices at the top of each source file
  6. Use International English for all user-facing text
  7. Follow POSIX standards for portability

Building from Git
-----------------

To build Twist from the Git repository:

  1. Ensure you have the following tools installed:
     - GNU autoconf
     - GNU automake
     - GNU libtool (if needed)
     - A C compiler (gcc recommended)
     - make

  2. Run the bootstrap script:
     ./bootstrap

  3. Configure and build:
     ./configure
     make

  4. Optionally run tests:
     make check

  5. Install (requires appropriate permissions):
     make install

Development Environment
----------------------

The following tools are recommended for development:

  - gcc or clang (C compiler)
  - gdb (debugger)
  - valgrind (memory checker)
  - GNU make
  - git (version control)

Contribution Agreement
----------------------

By contributing code to Twist, you agree to license your contributions
under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later.  You also
certify that:

  1. You have the right to submit the code under this license
  2. The code is your original work or you have obtained proper
     permission to submit it
  3. You grant a copyright license to the project maintainers

Maintainer Information
----------------------

The current maintainer of Twist is:

  Chris <chris@localhost>

If you have questions about development or want to discuss major
changes, please contact the maintainer.

